From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:57:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 55/72] Coordinate opt-in Engram validation before CUDA startup

Gather rank-local metadata results over the CPU bootstrap and retain its
sockets for session startup. Refuse every rank when a shard is invalid,
with the failing path and expected versus actual row geometry.

Cover asymmetric and simultaneous failures, retained-socket continuation,
canonical uneven partitions, padded bounds and contextual file errors.
Keep validation disabled by default and preserve the default startup path.
